%% Actual representative request: POST /api/work-orders.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Dispatcher
  participant Web as React web
  participant GW as YARP
  participant API as Work Order Service
  participant DB as Work Orders database
  participant Publisher as OutboxDispatcher
  participant Rabbit as RabbitMQ
  participant Consumer as Reporting / warehouse consumers
  Dispatcher->>Web: Create synthetic work order
  Web->>GW: POST /api/work-orders + bearer token
  GW->>API: Authenticated proxy request
  API->>API: Dispatch policy, team check, input validation
  API->>DB: Save order and WorkOrderCreated.v1 outbox row
  Note over API,DB: One owning-database transaction
  DB-->>API: Commit
  API-->>Web: 201 Created + order representation
  Publisher->>DB: Lock pending outbox rows
  Publisher->>Rabbit: Publish stable EventId
  Rabbit-->>Publisher: Broker confirmation
  Publisher->>DB: Mark published and commit
  Rabbit-->>Consumer: At-least-once delivery
  Consumer->>Consumer: Deduplicate event identity and update local read state
  Note over Web,Consumer: Committed command and analytical visibility have different timing.

